Responsibilities: 

- Work collaboratively with internal legal, commercial, and technical stakeholders as well as external counsel in drafting, reviewing and negotiating equipment supply and EPC contracts (and related services); 

- Manage multiple transactions; 

- Support the Execution, Operations and Asset Management teams during the construction and operational life cycle of the projects; 

- Facilitate legal support for cross-functional teams, focusing on regulatory compliance and strategic legal positioning; 

- Interface and negotiate directly with suppliers, EPCs, operators, and other counterparties as needed; 

- Oversee and manage external counsel in a wide range of matters; 

- Identify and succinctly communicate material risks and proposed solutions to Aypa’s executives and team leads; 

- Find ways to optimize and improve templates, processes for efficiency and compliance and apply best practices; 

- Other duties as assigned. 

Key Qualifications 

- JD from an accredited law school; 

- Active bar licensure in at least one US jurisdiction; 

- 5+ years of post-qualification experience, with demonstrated experience in utility-scale battery energy storage procurement, construction and operations; 

- Proven ability to manage multiple complex transactions and competing priorities; 

- Driven and takes ownership of deals to ensure timely execution and follow through; 

- Strong computer skills, including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint proficiency; 

- Excellent organizational and planning skills with meticulous attention to detail; 

- Exceptional written and verbal communication skills; 

- Strong interpersonal and diplomatic skills; 

- Highest standards of ethics and integrity. 

Compensation and Location: 

Salary: A base salary commensurate with experience. 

Bonus: An annual bonus will be awarded based on both individual performance as well as the overall success of the business. 

Benefits: Aypa offers an attractive benefits package with excellent health care/dental/vision, 401k matching, unlimited vacation, paid parental leave, and other health/wellness benefits. 

Location: Remote (USA). The ability to work in the United States is a requirement 

At Aypa, we nurture and support a highly diverse team and actively seek to advance fair and inclusive practices in all aspects of what we do. We hire passionate, dedicated, and forward-thinking individuals from different backgrounds and value unique perspectives and experiences. With a focus on belonging, we are committed to providing an inclusive environment for all. 

